findings.what:
In engine, hood, wooden face disc, cloth wraps, stone cape, staff and cup all render as one matte greige, chroma 3-8. The face disc sits only 5-15 L* under the hood. The approved concept separates them:
- chroma 10-18 (wood 16, wraps 17-18, stone 11-12);
- a face disc about 20-40 L* darker than the hood;
- a clear glass cup with the bead visible through it.
The signature prop is painted opaque into the body atlas: a white frosted cylinder under a dark slate cap. At portrait and splash size it reads as a lidded cup or a small bucket, not as glass holding light.
